# Approach
This solution uses Backtracking:
Place one queen per row
For each cell, check if placing a queen is safe
If safe, place the queen and move to the next row
If no valid placement exists, backtrack and try another column

# Key Functions
1.isSafe(...)
  Checks whether a queen can be placed at position (row, col) by verifying:
  Same row (horizontal)
  Same column (vertical)
  Upper-left diagonal
  Upper-right diagonal

2.nQueens(...)
  A recursive backtracking function that:
  Tries placing a queen in every column of the current row
  Stores the board when all n queens are successfully placed
  Backtracks if a placement leads to no solution

3.solveNQueens(int n)
  Initializes the board with '.'
  Calls the recursive backtracking function
  Returns all valid board configurations
